From a3c9a4a2061280b2915a455fcc1f376aafc270a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:52:39 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] ACPI: AC: defer probe until GenericSerialBus is ready

An AC adapter backed by a GenericSerialBus operation region can be probed before the corresponding I2C adapter has installed its address-space handler. In that case evaluating _PSR fails with AE_NOT_EXIST and the platform device remains permanently unbound.

Return -EPROBE_DEFER for this specific ACPICA status so the driver core retries the adapter after the serial-bus controller binds. Keep the existing -ENODEV result for permanent firmware errors.

Signed-off-by: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
---
 drivers/acpi/ac.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/ac.c b/drivers/acpi/ac.c
index f19d6dd43..f07ac866b 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/ac.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/ac.c
@@ -70,6 +70,8 @@ static int acpi_ac_get_state(struct acpi_ac *ac)
 				"Error reading AC Adapter state: %s\n",
 				acpi_format_exception(status));
 		ac->state = ACPI_AC_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
+		if (status == AE_NOT_EXIST)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
